---

A switch is the smallest kind of primitive: a fixed rule set with no slots, no tag form, no presets, and no value. It rides the same `data-ui` token list as everything else, so it stacks on a primitive (`data-ui="badge sr-only"`) or stands alone on a plain element.

{% switches /%}

## Pile

`pile` stacks every child in one grid cell, like layering with `position: absolute` but without taking anything out of flow. Pair it with `isolate` for a layered hero so the stacking context stays local: `data-ui="pile isolate"`.

{% preview src="utilities/pile" /%}

## Truncate

`truncate` keeps text on one line and ends the overflow with an ellipsis. It needs a width to overflow: a block element, a sized one (`--w: 48`), or a flex item with `--min-w: 0`, since a flex item can't shrink below its content otherwise. To clamp to more than one line, use the `--line-clamp` utility instead.

```html
<p data-ui="truncate">A file name far too long for its column.pdf</p>
```

## Animations

`spin`, `ping`, `pulse`, and `bounce` are Tailwind's looping animations: a spinner, a ping that scales out and fades (put it on a copy stacked behind a notification dot), a skeleton loader's slow fade, and a bounce for a scroll hint. They run on the kit's transition easing (`--default-transition-timing-function`) and stop when the visitor prefers reduced motion. They animate `transform`, so `--rotate`, `--scale`, and `--translate` still apply on top.

```html
<svg data-ui="spin" aria-hidden="true">…</svg>
<span data-ui="pile">
  <i
    data-ui="ping"
    style="
      --size: 2;
      --bg: var(--color-primary);
      --rounded: var(--radius-full);
    "
  ></i>
  <i
    style="
      --size: 2;
      --bg: var(--color-primary);
      --rounded: var(--radius-full);
    "
  ></i>
</span>
```

## Dividers

`divide-x` and `divide-y` draw a border between direct children. The container's `--divide` sizes or colors it with the border grammar: a number is pixels in `--color-border`, a color is 1px in that color, a length is the width.

## Group and container

`group` is listed with the [group modifier](/api/modifiers/group/) and `container` with [breakpoints](/api/foundations/breakpoints/); both are switches too.
